  "tldr": "For a Bernoulli experiment conducted on one growing connected sparse network generated by a stationary ergodic exponentially stabilizing iid-innovation rule, the exposure-IPW error splits exactly into a conditionally centered assignment coordinate and a Palm-population coordinate. The project derives their joint independent Gaussian limit, identifies \\(\\Omega_{\\mathrm{ann}}=\\Omega_{\\mathrm{des}}+\\Omega_{\\mathrm{pop}}\\), and asks the load-bearing random-metric question needed to prove that Leung's unchanged sample-mean-centered graph HAC estimates this full variance, with \\(R_n\\to\\Omega_{\\mathrm{pop}}\\). An exact local-chord cycle witnesses strict nondegeneracy, a common shock marks the nonergodic impossibility boundary, homogeneous effects recover the fixed-population result, and uniform Wald coverage supports a population-inference reanalysis of the randomized Facebook experiment of \\cite{BondEtAl2012} subject to data access and model diagnostics.",
  "project_justification": {
    "gap": "Theorem 4 and Remark 2 of \\cite{Leung2022ANI} interpret the sample-centered graph-HAC remainder as finite-population heterogeneity and leave its superpopulation limit model-dependent. Proposition 4.1 of \\cite{KojevnikovMarmerSong2021} proves HAC consistency after conditioning on a sigma-field containing the network, but its feasible centering does not cover deterministic heterogeneous conditional means generated by that same network. Stabilization and physical-dependence theorems in \\cite{BaryshnikovYukich2005} and \\cite{ElMachkouriVolnyWu2013} do not treat a quadratic selected by an endogenous shortest-path event.",
    "niche": "A stationary local-innovation model turns Leung's unidentifiable fixed-population remainder into a repeated-network population fluctuation, but only if the observed graph metric captures the corresponding Palm covariance without a persistent distance-selection term.",
    "fill": "The project proves the exact score split, derives the two variance limits and joint quenched--annealed Gaussian law from primitive uniform conditions, isolates and resolves the endogenous-random-metric quadratic with a four-root coupling, proves exactness of the unchanged HAC and uniform Wald coverage, and certifies the strict gain with explicit success and failure boundaries."
  },
  "related_work": "The writing arc follows \\cite{Leung2022ANI}, from misspecified local exposure mappings to ANI, exposure-IPW, and feasible graph-HAC inference; the changed target is the Palm population effect rather than the realized finite-network effect. Theorem 4 and Remark 2 in that paper are the direct comparator: the proposed exact-HAC theorem proves that its displayed \\(R_n\\) is the population component on a strict random-network subclass. Proposition 4.1 and its proof in \\cite{KojevnikovMarmerSong2021} provide the HAC decomposition into covariance-tail, stochastic four-tuple, and centering errors, but the proof conditions on the graph and begins with conditionally centered scores. Theorem 1 and the sample-autocovariance discussion in \\cite{ElMachkouriVolnyWu2013} provide the finite-radius physical-dependence projection and covariance-summability steps adapted to the environment score. The stabilization and Palm covariance machinery of \\cite{BaryshnikovYukich2005}, together with the quantitative dependency-graph truncation of \\cite{PenroseYukich2005}, informs the population CLT and the uniform normal approximation. \\cite{AbadieAtheyImbensWooldridge2020} supplies the econometric interpretation of distinct design and population uncertainties but not a network-interference score or HAC. \\cite{GaoDing2025} shows why a coverage theorem cannot be inferred from a pointwise design CLT and motivates the exactness diagnostic; its repair is deliberately conservative, whereas the present result asks when the unchanged estimator is exact for a broader target. \\cite{LiWager2022} gives a graphon population-target CLT and explicitly leaves difficult variance functionals, including a population heterogeneity term, without a feasible exact estimator. \\cite{AronowSamii2017} fixes exposure-probability and Horvitz--Thompson semantics under randomization. \\cite{Dedecker1998} motivates the invariant-common-shock mixed-limit boundary. The spatial HAC constructions of \\cite{Conley1999Spatial} and \\cite{KelejianPrucha2007} are the prespecified fallback if graph-distance selection is not neutral. Searches also located the recent network-misspecification estimator of \\cite{WeinsteinNevo2026} and the local-configuration estimator of \\cite{AuerbachGuoTabordMeehan2026}; their targets are robustness to an incorrectly specified network and nonparametric response prediction, respectively, not annealed variance estimation with an endogenous graph metric.",
  "technical_internal_limitation": "The local-chord calculation verifies one legal endogenous-metric example, not the uniform random-metric lemma. Two-sided chemical-distance capture controls gross metric mismatch but may still permit a shortest-path event to select endpoint innovations; the four-root proof must show that the aggregate selection term vanishes rather than assume it. If a stationary connected exponentially stabilizing counterexample leaves a persistent selection term, the unchanged-HAC theorem is false as stated and the project must pivot to an ambient spatial-distance HAC. The hard graph cutoff can also be indefinite in finite samples, so the proposal claims asymptotic ratio consistency and coverage, not finite-sample nonnegativity.",
  "honest_scope": "Every formal statement remains to be proved. The exact decomposition and witness arithmetic are feasibility receipts, not prior results. The central open content is \\(\\mathrm{oeq:endogenous\\mbox{-}random\\mbox{-}metric}\\); the headline exact-HAC and Wald theorems depend on its affirmative resolution. The common-shock construction lies outside the ergodic class and establishes a boundary rather than a covered case. Dense graphon sequences are not members of the sparse stabilizing class; only their assignment-dominated reduction is compared. The Facebook use is a proposed reanalysis of the randomized design reported by \\cite{BondEtAl2012}; no claim is made that the platform network satisfies stabilization, shell, chemical-distance, or Palm correspondence conditions without user-level graph and outcome access.",
